    <DataNode elementId="CPD-318" textLabel="monodehydroascorbate radical" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="LHFJOBMTAJJOTB-JLAZNSOCSA-N" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="200" centerY="780" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="xue, PMN, nilo-poyanco, SRI, caspi">|FRAME: ASCORBATE| is oxidized in cells to |FRAME: CPD-13907 dehydroascorbate| via the radical |FRAME: CPD-318|. |FRAME: CPD-13907 Dehydroascorbate| can be recycled back to ascorbate by the |FRAME: PWY-2261|, or it can be further broken down &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt; by irreversible reactions.</Comment>
